# NCE_NCE0103Y — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned in
# properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# NEW PART (2026-09-03, Middleweight diet). 100V / 3A N-channel MOSFET in SOT-23 for the
# sub-1A low-side outputs (holding brake coil, aux output) that were burning a 5x6 PDFN
# each (36.9mm2 -> 9.9mm2). Second FET part number on the board, accepted by Ben
# 2026-09-03 against the one-P/N rule. LCSC C153001, Extended, stock 13,634 @ $0.15
# (JLC parts API, 2026-09-03).
#
# DATASHEET FINDINGS (NCE NCE0103Y v1.0, read 2026-09-03): Vds 100V, Vgs +-20V, Id 3A,
# Idm 20A, Pd 1.5W, RthJA 100 K/W, Tj to 175C. Rds(on) 136 typ / 160 max mOhm @ 10V,
# 140 / 170 @ 4.5V; Vgs(th) 1.0-2.0V. Qg 20nC, Qgd 3.3nC @ 10V. Body diode Vsd 1.2V.
# Pinout G=1, S=2, D=3 (standard SOT-23). Gate is driven at 3.3V by the brake AND gate
# / the MCU: Vgs(th) max 2.0V leaves ~1.3V of enhancement, Rds at 3.3V is off the
# datasheet - budget ~250mOhm: brake 0.31A (0.62A at 200% overexcite) = 0.1W worst,
# aux 1A = 0.25W = 25K rise. Pin-compatible alternate with a first-tier brand: Diodes
# DMN10H220L-7 (C102615, 16.8k stock, 1.6A, 250mOhm @4.5V, Vgs(th) 1-2.5V).
G = io("G", Net, optional = True)
S = io("S", Net, optional = True)
D = io("D", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "NCE_NCE0103Y",
    footprint = File("NCE_NCE0103Y/SOT-23-3_L2.9-W1.6-P1.90-LS2.8-BR.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("NCE_NCE0103Y/NCE_NCE0103Y.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "Q",
    part = Part(mpn = "NCE0103Y", manufacturer = "Wuxi NCE Power Semiconductor"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C153001", "MPN": "NCE0103Y"},
    pins = {
        "G": G,
        "S": S,
        "D": D,
    },
)
